WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:05.200
The Iron Dome is hailed as the world’s&nbsp;
most effective air defense system,

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.760
boasting an interception success&nbsp;
rate of 90%, according to Israel.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.240
But recent events are challenging that perception.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.400
Hamas’ surprise attack is exposing&nbsp;
the system’s vulnerabilities.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.400
The Iron Dome can detect rockets&nbsp;
fired from 43 miles or 70 km away.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.760
It relies on a radar unit that detects when&nbsp;
a missile is launched and relays information

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.120
about its speed and trajectory to the control unit&nbsp;
- the brains of the system, which rapidly assesses

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.600
what kind of projectile is in the air and where it&nbsp;
could potentially land using advanced algorithms.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.640
Harmless trajectories are ignored. However, if&nbsp;
the control unit believes it’s heading for a

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.360
populated area or an area of strategic importance,&nbsp;
the launcher fires missiles to intercept the enemy

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.560
rocket by exploding near it while not making&nbsp;
direct contact with it. Each Iron Dome system,

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.160
often referred to as a “battery”, consists&nbsp;
of 3 or 4 launchers each equipped with

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.720
20 missiles. The system is mobile so&nbsp;
it can move to wherever it’s needed.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.080
Ten batteries are placed strategically throughout

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.840
the country, each defending an&nbsp;
area of up to 60 square miles.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.880
They don 't protect every inch of Israel’s&nbsp;
total area of 9,000 square miles. Instead,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.520
they’re strategically placed to&nbsp;
protect populated areas and key assets.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.840
If they didn’t exist, Israeli tanks would have

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.760
to roll into Gaza immediately to stop&nbsp;
the rocket fire like they did in 2009.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.040
To date, the U.S. has invested $2.6&nbsp;
billion in the Iron Dome defense system.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:42.120
The Iron Dome has been the backbone of&nbsp;
Israel’s multi-layered defense since 2011,

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.760
with thousands of successful interceptions.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:49.360
However, that backbone appeared&nbsp;
to crack on October 7th, 2023.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:55.120
Right now a massive barrage of rockets&nbsp;
coming off of the Gaza strip. This is

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:01.920
an effort by Hamas and Islamic jihad&nbsp;
to overhwelm Israel’s defense system.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:07.633
Whatever happened in the early hours of morning,&nbsp;
the iron dome was not able to stop this barrage.

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:11.280
The iron dome was not able to stop this barrage
The iron dome was not able to stop this barrage

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.800
Hamas unleashed an astonishing&nbsp;
number of rockets from Gaza:

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.920
they claim 5,000 in a span of 20 minutes.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.720
The Israeli Defense Forces&nbsp;
put the number at 2,200.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.480
Even taking the lower figure, the intensity of&nbsp;
this attack is remarkable when compared to the

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:33.200
50-day conflict in 2014, during which a total ofb&nbsp;
4,000 rockets were fired from Gaza into Israel.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.080
The Israeli Defense Forces have not&nbsp;
disclosed the number of rockets intercepted

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.000
However, evidence shows rockets&nbsp;
raining down on indiscriminate targets,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.760
leaving buildings destroyed&nbsp;
and hundreds of people dead.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.920
Iran’s state-affiliated Nour&nbsp;
News mockingly described the

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.840
Iron Dome as “nothing but a dome&nbsp;
of straw above a sand castle.”

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:59.800
The Iron Dome’s Tamir interceptors are neither&nbsp;
infinite nor cheap, costing around $50,000 each.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:04.520
In contrast, Hamas’ rudimentary Qassam&nbsp;
rockets that are fuelled by a mixture of

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:10.040
sugar and everyday fertilizer&nbsp;
cost $300 - $800 per launch.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.560
The sheer number of rockets Hamas was able&nbsp;
to secretly amass has led to questions.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.280
How did Israeli intelligence fail&nbsp;
to detect the growing stockpile?

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.320
It has one of the most advanced intelligence

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.689
agencies in the world and&nbsp;
works closely with the CIA.

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:23.720
It was an intelligence failure.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:28.480
Was Israel too preoccupied with other&nbsp;
threats like the more potent Hezbollah?

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.800
These are questions that Israeli&nbsp;
officials have so far failed to answer.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.960
The U.S. swiftly responded to the surprise

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.960
attacks by bolstering Israel’s&nbsp;
depleted Iron Dome interceptors.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:43.520
Since 2014, major American military&nbsp;
contractor Raytheon has partnered with

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:49.720
Israel’s Rafael Advanced Defense Systems to craft&nbsp;
components for the Tamir interceptor missiles.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.040
While the intention has been to support&nbsp;
Israel, this collaboration has also enhanced

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.960
U.S. defense capabilities. Two batteries&nbsp;
have been supplied to the U.S. Army.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.000
But faith in the Iron Dome isn’t universal.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.640
MIT professor Ted Postol who is an expert on

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.640
missile technology believes the Iron&nbsp;
Dome is not as reliable as it appears.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.960
He estimates its success rate during the November

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:17.560
2012 conflict between Israel and Hamas&nbsp;
might have been 5 percent or less.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.120
His evidence? Photographic documentation&nbsp;
of missile exhaust flight paths.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:25.600
For the Iron Dome missile to neutralize&nbsp;
an enemy rocket effectively, it should

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:30.720
confront it head-on. However, Professor Postol’s&nbsp;
research indicates the missiles often attacked

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:35.480
from the side which is a serious problem,&nbsp;
or from behind, which is also ineffective.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:40.280
In MIT Technology Review, he elaborates:&nbsp;
“If the interceptor hits the back end

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:46.240
of the rocket…the warhead will almost&nbsp;
certainly go on to the ground and explode.”

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.520
Professor Postol suggested that&nbsp;
the "Iron Dome radar tracking and

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.720
guidance system is not working" and&nbsp;
this sparked significant controversy.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.600
Israel's Ministry of Defence&nbsp;
dismissed his claims as "baseless",

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.120
maintaining their confidence in the Iron Dome.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.960
I reached out to Professor Postol&nbsp;
for his current take on the Iron

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.800
Dome's effectiveness but have not heard back.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:11.400
An intriguing sentiment from a 2021&nbsp;
Foreign Policy article suggests:

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:16.480
“...Israel’s air defenses may one day not&nbsp;
be enough to hinder volumes of rockets.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:21.800
Israel won’t admit this, but there is&nbsp;
a strategic peak for this technology.”

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.720
While the Iron Dome has kept Israel’s&nbsp;
citizens safe for over a decade,

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.840
it’s clearly not infallible.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.240
The recent surprise attacks reveal&nbsp;
the cracks in the Iron Dome,

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:37.000
underscoring that even the world’s most&nbsp;
advanced defense system…has its limits.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.240
As we discuss advanced defense&nbsp;
technologies like the Iron Dome,

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:45.520
one can't help but wonder about the historical&nbsp;
events that necessitate such innovations.

